# package shapes

A package's doc comment opens the package's page.

## Point

```loke
Point :: struct {
	/// Across, in metres.
	x: f64,
	y: f64,
	// and fields private to the package
}
```

A point on the plane.

## Handle

```loke
Handle :: struct {
	// and fields private to the package
}
```

Opaque to importers.

## Facing

```loke
Facing :: enum { North, South }
```

## Turn

```loke
Turn :: enum { Left, Right }
```

A block doc comment loses the indentation its lines share.

Its blank lines stay,
	and so does deeper indentation.

## Lane

```loke
Lane :: enum { Inner, Outer }
```

## MAX_SIDE

```loke
MAX_SIDE :: 1000
```

The largest side any shape may have.

## make_point

```loke
make_point :: proc(x: f64, y: f64) -> Point
```

## LIMIT

```loke
LIMIT :: 10
```

## square_area

```loke
@(require_results)
square_area :: proc(side: f64) -> f64
```

The area of a square with `side`.
It is always non-negative.

## Point.sum

```loke
sum :: proc(self) -> f64
```

The sum of the coordinates.

## LONGEST

```loke
LONGEST :: units.METRE * MAX_SIDE
```

The longest side, in metres.

# package units (`./units`)

Lengths, in metres. `-doc` gives each package of the project its own page,
after the root's.

## METRE

```loke
METRE :: 1.0
```

One metre.
